==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Babel the Darkflame''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''God-Emperor Babel''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Sadly for the Legend Rare of the Dragon Emperors, High Lord Babel is riddled with flaws. Babel costs an absurd 6750¢, the second-highest out of any unit in the game. This is dragged down by a very slow recharge time of over 150s, around twice of that of the average tanker. And while his damage per hit is actually respectable, it is dragged down by a long foreswing, making his damage output unreliable. With the effectiveness of [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], one might wonder if High Lord Babel could put in any work for players lucky enough to have him.

Thankfully, he can. Babel's defining advantage is his colossal health of 255K at Lv.30 (405K at Lv.50). However, thanks to Babel's [[Insanely Tough|Insane Toughness]] against Red and Floating, he takes 1/7 the damage from them, giving him an unmatched 1.78M effective HP against them at Lv.30, and 2.83M effective HP at Lv.50. This allows him to hold off even the toughest Red/Floating threats, and trade hits with ranged attackers like [[Professor A.]] Babel still does not have the efficiency of Roe and Octopus, so he makes up for it with Immunities to Freeze and Slow, improving his sturdiness as a tank. Another unique aspect of Babel is his range of 390. While it seems counterintuitive for a tank to have range as it prevents them from tanking for melee and midranged attackers, what this does is allow Babel to function as a midranged defensive layer, standing behind your meatshields but still being able to protect backliners.

Despite his massive HP, Babel should not be treated as a damage sponge left exposed to enemy attackers. Red/Floating enemies are very aggressive and could tear through his HP surprisingly quickly if he is left exposed. Instead, treat Babel like a second layer of defense. Your meatshields and Roe/Octopus Cats would still do the brunt of the tanking, but when your frontline defenses get breached, Babel comes in to hold the line until the enemy pushers are dealt with. When used this way, Babel could feel unkillable against his target traits and even synergise, rather than compete, with Roe Cat and Octopus Cat.

While Babel's extreme cost and lengthy cooldown makes him an unreliable generalist, if you're lucky to roll him in early game, he can be used as a much tankier [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]]. Babel has the exact same damage as Bahamut, a faster attack frequency, and a whopping TEN TIMES the health compared to Bahamut, but has considerably less range.

==='''True Form'''===
While Babel's True Form does not revolutionise him, he still gains several buffs that improve his prowess as a tanker. The first notable enhancement is his 20% HP increase, improving his ability to tank his target traits. More significantly, he becomes immune to both knockback and toxic, which resolves problems usually plaguing slow tanks like him. The Toxic immunity allows him to completely wall [[Gobble]] and [[Zollow]], making him a hard-counter to them. His Knockback immunity helps reinforce his sturdiness and improves his matchups into enemies like [[The Red Malice]], [[Red EnerG]] and possibly [[Masked Okame]]. His Colossus Slayer, on the other hand, is not as important; Babel has very few viable matchups due to his not-so-great offense and overall variety in Colossus Gauntlet design, limiting him to fighting [[J.J. Jackrabbit]] by countering its knockback effect and exploiting its dual-type weakness. Overall, this True Form is not a massive buff, but is a good improvement to Babel.

